I can breathe better in his 301 section &#128517;
Okay guys, lets start praying for TT2. In full fairness, his questions during help session were quite fair and he even went over calculations. He even said he was worried since most of the class didn't show up. Oh well, good luck to them. But as for the lecture, A+
He seems like a sweet guy

Great professor, very lucky to have such a professor in my first math class in uoft.
 Understanding and funny lecture, even after 3 years he still answered the questions I was wondering about.
 Always recommend&#65281;

Excerpt from our PHY356 piazza (class forum with instructors). 

&#8220;I feel that the harm caused to the student body is detrimental and unrecognized. If you believe this is dramatic, it is, but justly so. I implore you to see how many graduate schools accept applicants with a D- in 3rd year QM.&#8221;

Course average was 60%. No curve. Avoid at all costs.

Professor Stangeby is a memorable professor. I am taking ESC 194 currently and I feel deeply sorry for the loss of such a great professor. I could still remember the "Chat? Email me." on the chalkboard, but I can never reach out again.
I would like to use this ancient Chinese poem as mourning:
